      "description": "Watch Inter vs Napoli highlights and goals from Serie A on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 5, 2026. Two of Serie A's heavyweights produced a memorable spectacle at the San Siro that kept fans on the edge of their seats until the final whistle. The match on September 5, 2026, became a testament to the unpredictable nature of top-tier football, as the momentum swung wildly between the two sides. Tactical Stalemate in the Opening Period The contest began with Inter attempting to establish dominance on home turf, frequently utilizing Federico Dimarco and Nicolo Barella to deliver dangerous crosses from corner situations. Despite the sustained pressure, the SSC Napoli backline remained disciplined and organized. The most significant opening of the first half arrived in the 12th minute when Francesco Pio Esposito directed a powerful header toward goal, only to be denied by a sharp save from Alex Meret . The first 45 minutes concluded goalless, characterized by intense midfield duels and a tactical yellow card for Antonio Vergara , who halted a promising counter-attack. Napoli Strike Twice as the Game Ignites The second half exploded into life shortly after the restart. In the 50th minute, a defensive lapse by Nicolo Barella proved costly as Matteo Politano reacted quickest to a loose ball, firing home with his right foot to give the visitors the lead. The San Siro was stunned again just three minutes later when Rasmus Højlund unleashed a brilliant long-range strike from outside the box, assisted by Giovanni Di Lorenzo , to double the advantage. However, Inter responded almost immediately. In the 56th minute, Federico Dimarco turned provider for Lautaro Martínez , who clinical finished with his right foot to pull one back and ignite the comeback. A Thrilling Turn of Events and Late Drama As the clock ticked down, tactical changes altered the course of the match. Inter introduced Carlos Augusto and Marcus Thuram , a combination that proved decisive in the 82nd minute when Augusto's precise cross found Thuram for a commanding header to level the scores. The drama reached its crescendo in stoppage time. In the 91st minute, Manuel Akanji played a key role in setting up Lautaro Martínez , who struck again—this time with his left foot—to complete the sensational turnaround. The emotions ran high as Cristian Chivu was booked for his exuberant celebrations, marking the end of a classic Serie A encounter."
